          %p
            %br/
          %h3#IdeaGraphComplexModelForSpacesOfKnots Model for spaces of knots
          %p
            The graph complex model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+knots"} spaces of knots
            was originally sketched in
            %a{:href => "#Kontsevich93"} Kontsevich 93, Section 5
            and worked out in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CattaneoCottaRamusinoLongoni02"} Cattaneo, Cotta-Ramusino, Longoni 02
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CattaneoCottaRamusinoLongoni05"} 05
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BarNatan91"} Bar-Natan 91
          %p
            Here we denote this version of the graph complex by “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KnotGraphs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KnotGraphs
            ”, in contrast to “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Graphs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs
            ” for the other model, discussed
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#IdeaGraphComplexModelsForConfigurationSpacesOfPoints"} above
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AKnotGraphInTheKnotGraphComplexII.jpg", :width => "190"}/
          %p
            The explicit definition is almost exactly the same as that of the model for configuration spaces of points
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#IdeaGraphComplexModelsForConfigurationSpacesOfPoints"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
            between consecutive external vertices, often called
            = succeed "," do
              %em arcs
          %p
            Together these two innocent modifications make the graphs now represent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+amplitude"} vacuum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            in the presence of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop"} Wilson loop
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot"} knot
            (corresponding to the dashed line shown on the right):
