          %p
            %br/
          %h3#model_for_other_spaces Model for other spaces
          %p
            There are yet other, inequivalent, graph complexes. Notably there is a type of graph complex whose (co)homology in degree 0 is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck-Teichm%C3%BCller+group"} Grothendieck-Teichmüller group
            (
            %a{:href => "#Willwacher10"}> Willwacher 10
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#DolgushevRogers12"} Dolgushev-Rogers 12
          %h2#GraphComplex Definition
          %h3#OverviewOfDefinitions Overview
          %p
            There are two different classes of (Kontsevich-) graph complexes, modelling the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            of, respectively,
