                  }{
                  \\underbrace{
                  \\underset{{}^{1,\cdots,n}}{Conf}(\Sigma)
                  }
                  }
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The full graph complexes/configuration spaces are just the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of those for fixed number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            of external vertices/points, hence one may focus attention on the latter.
          %p
            The precise form of these relations is the content of the theorems discussed below. Before stating this in detail, we make some general remarks on how the situation depends on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
            Beware that the graphs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma] \in Graphs_n(\Sigma)
            themselves are
            %em not
            going to carry an embedding into the manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlator+as+differential+form+on+configuration+space+of+points"} correlator
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            on the space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
            As a consequence, the dependence of the graph complexes themselves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is mild:
          %p
            In particular, in the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = \mathbb{R}^D
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Graphs
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs\big( \mathbb{R}^D \big)
            depend essentially only on whether the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/odd+number"} odd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^D)
            is
          #eq:DegreeOfAGraph.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi deg
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo #
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mi Edges
                  %mo −
                  %mi D
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo #
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Vertices
                    %mi int
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  deg\big( [\Gamma]\big)
                  \\;=\;
                  (D-1) \cdot \#\!Edges - D \cdot \#\!Vertices_{int}
                  \\,,
          %p
            hence each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edge"} edge
            contributes a degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D-1
            and each internal vertex a degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} sign rule
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded-commutative+algebra"} graded-commutative algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^D)
            we have the following parities
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = \mathbb{R}^D
                %th edges
                %th internal vertices
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  even
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} odd
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} even
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  odd
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} even
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} odd
          %p
            Up to an absolute
            %em even
            change of grading, the graph complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^D)
            depend only on these parities, hence depend only on whether
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/odd+number"} odd
          %p
            Finally, beware that many authors consider the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = \mathbb{R}^D
            by default, and don’t mention a dependence on a choice of manifold, but just on a natural number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p For instance:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the “graph complex with anti-symmetric set of edges” of
                %a{:href => "#BarNatanMcKay"} Bar-Natan &amp; McKay, Def. 3.3
                is denoted
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi GC
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GC_2
                in
                %a{:href => "#Willwacher10"} Willwacher 10
                and is our
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Graphs
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_0\big(\mathbb{R}^2\big)
            %li
              %p
                similarly
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi GC
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GC_3
                in
                %a{:href => "#KoroshkinWillwacherZivkovic14"} Koroshkin-Willwacher-Živković 14
                is our
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi KnotGraphs
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KnotGraphs\big( \mathbb{R}^3\big)
          %p
            (While the cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_0(\Sigma)
            – being equivalent to that of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Conf
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conf_0(\Sigma) \simeq \ast
            – is trivial, these authors consider further filtrations which have non-trivial cohomology in filtration stages, see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BarNatanMcKay"} Bar-Natan &amp; McKay, Def. 3.6
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#GraphComplexesModellingConfigurationSpacesOfPoints
            %strong 1)
            Graph complexes modelling configuration spaces of points
          %p
            We discuss graph complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_n(\Sigma)
            modelling the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi Conf
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{{}^{1,\cdots,n}}{Conf}(\Sigma)
          %p
            For the case of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = \mathbb{R}^D
            these were originally hinted at in
            %a{:href => "#Kontsevich92"} Kontsevich 92 (p. 11-12)
            and discussed in detail in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volić 14
          %p
            %br/
          %h4#GraphComplexForConfigurationsOfPointsInR3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3 \big)
          %p
            We state the definition of the graph complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3\big)
            (as motivated
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#IdeaGraphComplexModelsForConfigurationSpacesOfPoints"} above
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GraphComplexDgcAlgebra"}
            below) associated with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            3, following
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volić 14, Section 6
          %h5#graphs Graphs
          #Graphs.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (graphs)
            %p
              In the following, by a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
              we mean specifically:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Edg
                        %munderover
                          %mo ⇉
                          %mi t
                          %mi s
                        %mi Vert
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Edg \underoverset{t}{s}{\rightrightarrows} Vert
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  a decomposition of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Vert
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vert
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
                  as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Vert
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi Vert
                          %mi ext
                        %mo ⊔
                        %msub
                          %mi Vert
                          %mi int
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Vert \simeq Vert_{ext} \sqcup Vert_{int}
                %p of “external” and “internal” vertices.
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Vert
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vert
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Vert
                            %mi ext
                          %mo &lt;
                          %msub
                            %mi Vert
                            %mi int
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vert_{ext} \lt Vert_{int}
            %p
              Hence both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vert_{ext}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vert_{int}
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+orders"} linear orders
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Vert
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mo &lt;
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Vert = Vert_{ext} \sqcup_{{}_{\lt}} Vert_{int}
            %p
              is their ordered
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \simeq \Gamma'
              of such graphs is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijections"} bijections
              between sets of edges and vertices
            #eq:IsomorphismOfGraphs.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Edg
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⇉
                              %mi t
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Vert
                              %mi ext
                            %mo ⊔
                            %msub
                              %mi Vert
                              %mi int
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mo ≃
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mo ≃
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Edg
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⇉
                              %mrow
                                %mi t
                                %mo ′
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mi Vert
                            %msub
                              %mo ′
                              %mi ext
                            %mo ⊔
                            %mi Vert
                            %msub
                              %mo ′
                              %mi int
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Edg &amp;\underoverset{t}{s}{\rightrightarrows}&amp; Vert_{ext} \sqcup Vert_{int}
                    \\\
                    \\mathllap{{}^{\simeq}}\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\mathllap{{}^{\simeq}}\big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    Edg' &amp;\underoverset{t'}{s'}{\rightrightarrows}&amp; Vert'_{ext} \sqcup Vert'_{int}
                    }
            %p
              which respects all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
              maps, the decomposition into external and internal vertices, and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Def. 6.1
            )
          #EmptyGraph.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+graph"}> empty graph
                )
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+graph"} empty graph
              counts as a graph, according to Def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
          %p
            We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mi Vert
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo |
                    %mi Vert
                    %mo |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#\! Vert \coloneqq \left\vert Vert \right\vert
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            of the sets of vertices, etc.
          #DenotationForLinearOrderOnVertices.num_defn
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong (denotation for linear order on vertices)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
              in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              is equivalently a choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Vert
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vert
              with the set of the first
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo #
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mi Vert
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#\!Vert
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            #eq:NaturalNumberLabelsOfVertices.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Vert
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mo #
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                    %mo ,
                    %mo #
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mo #
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                    %mo +
                    %mo #
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Vert
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\big\{
                    1, 2, \ldots, \# Vert_{ext}, \# Vert_{ext} + 1, \ldots , \# Vert_{ext} + \# Vert_{int}
                    \\big\}
            %p With this understood, we may depict graphs as as diagrams with oriented edges and numbered vertices.
          #DegreeOfAGraph.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (degree of a graph)
            %p Given a graph
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Edg
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi t
                      %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                    %mo ⊔
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma
                    \\;=\;
                    \\big(
                    Edg
                    \\underoverset{t}{s}{\rightrightarrows}
                    Vert_{ext}
                    \\sqcup
                    Vert_{int}
                    \\big)
            %p
              according to Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              %em degree
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo #
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mi Edg
                    %mo −
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo #
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    deg(\Gamma)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    2 \cdot \#\!Edg
                    \-
                    3 \cdot \#\!Vert_{int}
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence the sum of 2 for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edge"} edge
              and of -3 for each internal
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex"} vertex
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Def. 6.6
            )
          %p If we also agree to
          %ol
            %li
              %p denote internal vertices by a bullet;
            %li
              %p
                denote external vertices by…
                %em no
                denotation (as usual for
                = succeed "!)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
          %p then the ingredients of these graphs are as shown in the following figure:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/GraphComplexIngredients.jpg", :width => "880"}/
          %p The following shows some very simple examples of graphs, depicted this way:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SomeExamplesOfGraphs.jpg", :width => "610"}/
          %p
            %strong Beware
            that graphs need not be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+graph"} planar
          %p
            In particular, graphs may have
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpoles"} tadpoles
          #SignRulesForGraphs.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (sign rules for graphs)
            %p
              For a fixed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Vert
                        %mi ext
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mo #
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Vert
                        %mi ext
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vert_{ext} \simeq \{1, 2, \cdots, \#\!Vert_{ext}\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} linear span
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:IsomorphismOfGraphs"} (4)
              of graphs, according to Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            #eq:LinearSpanOfIsoClassesOfGraphs.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} [
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %mi Edg
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi t
                      %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                    %mo ⊔
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi FinLinOrd
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}
                    \\Big[
                    \\big\{
                    Edg
                    \\underoverset{t}{s}{\rightrightarrows}
                    Vert_{ext}
                    \\sqcup
                    Vert_{int}
                    \\;\vert\;
                    Vert_{int} \in FinLinOrd
                    \\big\}_{/\sim}
                    \\Big]
                    \\;\in\;
                    Vect_{\mathbb{R}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The degree associated with a graph (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegreeOfAGraph"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
            %p
              On this
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
              generated by
            #eq:SignFromOrientationReversal.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (7)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ′
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ′
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext is
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi Γ
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext with
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext orientation of one edge reversed
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma
                    \\;\sim\;
                    \-\Gamma'
                    \\phantom{AA}
                    \\array{
                    \\text{if}\;\Gamma'\; \text{is}\;\Gamma\;\text{with}
                    \\\
                    \\text{orientation of one edge reversed}
                    }
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/GraphComplexSignsFromOrientationReversal.jpg", :width => "400"}/
            %p and
            #eq:SignRuleFromOrderingInternalVertices.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (8)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ′
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ′
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext is
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi Γ
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext with
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext a pair of consecutive internal vertices transposed
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma
                    \\;\sim\;
                    \-\Gamma'
                    \\phantom{AA}
                    \\array{
                    \\text{if}\;\Gamma'\;\text{is}\;\Gamma\;\text{with}
                    \\\
                    \\text{a pair of consecutive internal vertices transposed}
                    }
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Def. 6.5 &amp; Def. 6.5
            )
          %p
            Since this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            is linear, the set of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            is still a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegreeOfAGraph"}
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
          #GradedVectorSpaceOfGraphs.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong (graded vector space of graphs)
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo #
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Vert
                        %mi ext
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \coloneqq \#\! Vert_{ext}
            #eq:VectorSpaceOfGraphsWithSignRulesImposed.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (9)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} [
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %mi Edg
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi s
                      %mi t
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                    %mo ⊔
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi int
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi FinLinOrd
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat{Graphs}_n\big(\mathbb{R}^3\big)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\mathbb{R}
                    \\Big[
                    \\big\{
                    Edg
                    \\underoverset{s}{t}{\rightrightarrows}
                    Vert_{ext}
                    \\sqcup
                    Vert_{int}
                    \\;\vert\;
                    Vert_{int} \in FinLinOrd
                    \\big\}_{/\sim}
                    \\Big]_{/\sim}
                    \\;\in\;
                    Vect_{\mathbb{R}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              under the sign rules
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SignFromOrientationReversal"} (7)
              and
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SignRuleFromOrderingInternalVertices"} (8)
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} linear span
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LinearSpanOfIsoClassesOfGraphs"} (6)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of graphs (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              external vertices.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              any graph, we write
            #eq:EquivalenceClassOfAGraphForSignRules.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (10)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big[ \Gamma \big]
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\widehat{Graphs}_n\big(\mathbb{R}^3\big)
                    \\,.
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
              of the element in this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              that it represents.
            %p
              When there is not risk of confusion, we will still refer to this equivalence class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma]
              as a
              = succeed "." do
                %em graph
          %p
            A further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Graphs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi Graphs
                      %mo ^
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VectorSpaceOfGraphsWithSignRulesImposed"} (9)
            will underly the actual graph complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#TheGraphComplex"} below
          #GraphsWithDirectLoopsVanish.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong (no tadpoles)
            %p
              A direct consequence of quotienting out the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SignFromOrientationReversal"} (7)
              is that graphs with “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpoles"}> tadpoles
              ”, namely with edges that have coinciding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex"} vertex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VectorSpaceOfGraphsWithSignRulesImposed"} (9)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Edg
                      %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext s.t.
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    e \in Edg_\Gamma
                    \\;\text{s.t.}\;
                    s(e) = t(e)
                    \\phantom{AA}
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\phantom{AA}
                    \\big[ \Gamma \big]
                    \\;=\;
                    0
            %p
              (This holds more generally for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^D
              with odd
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D  = 2k + 1
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/GraphsWithDirectLoopsVanishInTheGraphComplex.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          #TrivalenGraphs.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong (trivalent graphs)
            %p
              A graph without external vertices has degree (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegreeOfAGraph"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo #
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Verts
                      %mi ext
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext all vertices are trivalent
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\#\!Verts_{ext} = 0
                    \\;\;\Rightarrow\;\;
                    \\big(
                    deg(\Gamma) = 0
                    \\;\;\Leftrightarrow\;\;
                    \\text{all vertices are trivalent}
                    \\big)
                    \\,.
            %p The following is the smallest example of such a trivalent graph:
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/TheDegreeZeroGraph.jpg", :width => "240"}/
            %p Hence in general, the degree of a trivalent graph is three times its number of external vertices:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext trivalent
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo #
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Verts
                      %mi ext
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma
                    \\;
                    \\text{trivalent}
                    \\;\;\;\Rightarrow \;\;\;
                    deg\big( [\Gamma] \big)
                    \\;=\;
                    3 \cdot \#\!Verts_{ext}
                    \\,.
            %p (Because such a graph is the result of taking a trivalent graph in degree 0 and replacing internal vertices of degree -3 with external vertices of degree 0.)
            %p
              For example, the following graph, obtained from the above trivalent graph by replacing the three internal vertices labeled 1,2 and 3 with external vertices, is of degree
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mn 3
                      %mo =
                      %mn 9
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3 \cdot 3 = 9
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ATrivalentGraphOfDegree9.jpg", :width => "240"}/
          %p
            %br/
          %h5#the_algebra_of_graphs The algebra of graphs
          #WedgeProductOfGraphs.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (wedge product of graphs)
            %p For
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\Gamma_1], [\Gamma_2]
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\widehat Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^D\big)
            %p
              two equivalence classes
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VectorSpaceOfGraphsWithSignRulesImposed"} (9)
              of isomorphism classes of graphs (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GradedVectorSpaceOfGraphs"}
              %em wedge product
              is the element
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\Gamma_1] \wedge [\Gamma_2]
                    \\coloneqq
                    [\Gamma_1 \wedge \Gamma_2]
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\widehat Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^D\big)
            %p
              represented by the graph (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+orders"} linear orders
              of edges and
              %em internal
              vertices
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Edgs
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mo &lt;
                    %msub
                      %mi Edgs
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 2
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊔
                          %mo &lt;
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊔
                          %mo &lt;
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mo &lt;
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mrow
                        %mi int
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mo &lt;
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mrow
                        %mi int
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_1 \wedge \Gamma_2
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\Big(
                    Edgs_{\Gamma_1}
                    \\sqcup_{{}_{\lt}}
                    Edgs_{\Gamma_2}
                    \\underoverset{t_1 \sqcup_{\lt} t_2}{s_1 \sqcup_{\lt} s_2}{\rightrightarrows}
                    Vert_{ext}
                    \\sqcup_{{}_{\lt}}
                    \\big(
                    Vert_{int,1}
                    \\sqcup_{{}_{\lt}}
                    Vert_{int,2}
                    \\big)
                    \\Big)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, 6.3
            )
          %p It is immediate that:
          #GradedCommutativeAlgebraOfGraphs.num_defn
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong (graded commutative algebra of graphs)
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3\big)
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VectorSpaceOfGraphsWithSignRulesImposed"} (9)
              of graphs (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GradedVectorSpaceOfGraphs"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeProductOfGraphs"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi Graphs
                                %mo ^
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi Graphs
                                %mo ^
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ∧
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi Graphs
                                %mo ^
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\widehat{Graphs}_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
                    \\otimes
                    \\widehat{Graphs}_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
                    \&amp;\overset{\wedge}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\widehat{Graphs}_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
                    \\\
                    \\big(
                    [\Gamma_1], [\Gamma_2]
                    \\big)
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    [\Gamma_1 \wedge \Gamma_2]
                    }
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded-commutative+algebra"} graded-commutative algebra
          %p
            %br/
          %h5#TheDifferential The differential on graphs
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            on the graded vector space of equivalence classes of graphs
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VectorSpaceOfGraphsWithSignRulesImposed"} (9)
            is defined in terms of contraction of certain edges in the graph (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractionOfAnEdge"}
            below). For this we first say which edges count as
            %em contractible
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractibleEdges"}
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SignOfAContractibleEdge"}
          #ContractibleEdges.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              %strong (contractible edges)
            %p
              Given a graph
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edge"} edge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Edg
                      %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in Edg_\Gamma
              is a
              %em contractible edge
              if the following conditions hold:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  is not a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole"} tadpole
                  (Example
                  = succeed "):" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GraphsWithDirectLoopsVanish"}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≠
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        s(e) \neq t(e)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  has at least one internal vertex:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Vert
                          %mi int
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                        %mtext or
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Vert
                          %mi int
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        s(e) \in Vert_{int}
                        \\phantom{AA}
                        \\text{or}
                        \\phantom{AA}
                        t(e) \in Vert_{int}
              %li
                %p
                  every internal vertex of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  is connected to more than just one other vertex, i.e.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  is
                  %em not
                  a solid arrow in a diagram of the following form
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DeadEndsInGraphComplex.jpg", :width => "570"}/
            %p We write
            #eq:SetOfContractibleEdges.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (11)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Edg
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi contr
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Egd
                      %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Edg^{contr}_\Gamma
                    \\;\subset\;
                    Egd_\Gamma
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              of the contractible edges inside all edges of a graph
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, p. 60
            )
          #ContractionOfAnEdge.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              %strong (contraction of an edge)
            %p
              Given a graph
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Edg
                      %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in Edg_\Gamma
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractibleEdges"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi e
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Edg
                      %mi Γ
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi Γ
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi max
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma / e
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\big(
                    Edg_\Gamma
                    \\setminus \{e\}
                    \\big)
                    \\underoverset{q \circ t}{q \circ s}{\rightrightarrows}
                    \\big(
                    Vert_\Gamma
                    \\setminus \{ max(s(e),t(e))  \}
                    \\big)
            %p and connecting all edges previously attached with the removed vertex to the remaining vertex of that edge (ie. the one with the smaller label):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Vert
                              %mi Γ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Vert
                              %mrow
                                %mi Γ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi e
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi v
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi min
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi s
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi e
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi e
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mtd
                                      %mtext if
                                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                      %mi v
                                      %mo =
                                      %mi max
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi s
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi e
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi e
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi v
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mtd
                                      %mtext otherwise
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Vert_\Gamma &amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Vert_{\Gamma/e}
                    \\\
                    v &amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    min(s(e),t(e)) &amp;\vert&amp; \text{if}\; v = max(s(e),t(e))
                    \\\
                    v &amp;\vert&amp; \text{otherwise}
                    }
                    \\right.
                    }
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Def. 6.9
            )
          #SignOfAContractibleEdge.num_defn
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong (sign of a contractible edge)
            %p
              Given a
              %em contractible edge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Egd
                      %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in Egd_\Gamma
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractibleEdges"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %mi t
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi e
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mi s
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %mi s
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi e
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi s
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon(e)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    (-1)^{ t(e) } &amp;\vert&amp; t(e) \gt s(e)
                    \\\
                    \-(-1)^{s(e)} &amp;\vert&amp; s(e) \gt t(e)
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right we are identifying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
              on the vertices with their
              = succeed "-labels" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:NaturalNumberLabelsOfVertices"} (5)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, p. 65
            )
          #DifferentialOnGraphs.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              %strong (differential on graphs)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vert_{ext}
              a fixed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mo #
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Vert
                      %mi ext
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = \#\! Vert_{ext}
              external vertices, define on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3\big)
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VectorSpaceOfGraphsWithSignRulesImposed"} (9)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              given on the class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma]
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EquivalenceClassOfAGraphForSignRules"} (10)
              of a graph
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
              of all its edge contractions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma/e
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractionOfAnEdge"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractibleEdges"}
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SignOfAContractibleEdge"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi Graphs
                                %mo ^
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi Graphs
                                %mo ^
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi e
                                %mo ∈
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi Edg
                                  %mi Γ
                                  %mi contr
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\widehat Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3\big)
                    \&amp;\overset{d}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\widehat Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3\big)
                    \\\
                    [\Gamma]
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\underset{ e \in Edg^{contr}_\Gamma }{\sum}
                    \\epsilon(\Gamma) \cdot [\Gamma/e]
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, (84)
            )
          #DifferentialOnLinearGraph.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              %strong (differential of propagator graph vanishes)
            %p
              The differential from Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOnGraphs"}
              vanishes on all graphs without any internal vertices (since these have no contractible edges in the sense of Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractibleEdges"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+propagator"} Chern-Simons propagator
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DifferentialOnPropagatorGraphVanishes.jpg", :width => "270"}/
          #DifferentialOnLinearGraph.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              %strong (differential on linear graphs)
            %p
              The differential of Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOnGraphs"}
              applied to the linear graph with one internal vertex:
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DifferentialOfSimpleLinearGraphInGraphComplex.jpg", :width => "700"}/
            %p
              Here the right hand side vanishes, due to the sign rule
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SignFromOrientationReversal"} (7)
            %p
              While this example illustrates the general action of the differential, beware that this particular differential relation will not actually contribute to the graph complex, as the graph on the left is a “vanishing graph” in the sense of Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanishingGraphs"}
              below (since the valence of the internal vertex is
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt 3
          #ThreeTermRelation.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              %strong (differential of trivalent diagram with single internal vertex)
            %p
              The image of the single trivalent internal vertex under the differential from Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOnGraphs"}
              is as shown in the following:
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DifferentialOfSingleTrivalentInternalVertex.jpg", :width => "800"}/
            %p
              Under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheQuasiIsomorphism"} (1)
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+compactification"} Fulton-MacPherson compactification
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
              to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+propagator"} Chern-Simons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitude+on+compactified+configuration+spaces+of+points"} Feynman amplitude on compactified configuration spaces of points
              (
              %a{:href => "Fulton-MacPherson+operad#QuasiIsomorphismBetweenGraphComplexAndDeRhamComplexOfFM"}> this Prop.
              ), this relation becomes the “3-term relation” (
              %a{:href => "Fulton-MacPherson+operad#DeRhamCohomologyOfFMCompactification"}> this Prop.
              ):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo ]
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo ]
                    %mo +
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo ]
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mi i
                      %mo ]
                    %mo +
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mi i
                      %mo ]
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left[g_{i j}\right] \wedge \left[ g_{j k} \right]
                    +
                    \\left[g_{j k}\right] \wedge \left[ g_{k i} \right]
                    +
                    \\left[g_{k i}\right] \wedge \left[ g_{i j} \right]
                    \\;\sim\;
                    0
            %p
              satisfied by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+propagator"} Chern-Simons propagator
              form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi PA
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                      %munder
                        %mi Conf
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi D
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    g_{i j}
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\Omega^2_{PA}
                    \\Big(
                    \\underset{{}^{1,\cdots,n}}{Conf}
                    \\big(
                    \\mathbb{R}^D
                    \\big)
                    \\Big)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Figure 1 and 2
            )
          #DifferentialOfMinimalTrivalenVacuumGraph.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (Differential of minimal trivalent
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+diagram"} vacuum diagram
            %p
              The differential of the minimum trivalent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+diagram"} vacuum diagram
              from Example
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivalenGraphs"}
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/The0CocycleInTheGraphComplex.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          #DifferentialOfTrivalentTreeWithTwoInternalVertices.num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p
              %strong (differential of trivalent tree with two internal vertices)
            %p
              The differential (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOnGraphs"}
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DiffTrivTreeWthTwoIntVertices.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          #DifferentialProperties.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              %strong (differential graded algebra structure)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOnGraphs"}
              makes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^D)
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              from Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GradedCommutativeAlgebraOfGraphs"}
              in fact a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebra"} differential graded algebra
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (well defined)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                  indeed only depends on the equivalence class
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma]
              %li
                %p
                  (degree)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                  increases degree by +1
              %li
                %p (nilpotency)
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d \circ d = 0
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"}> derivation
                  )
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi deg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d( [\Gamma_1] \wedge [\Gamma_2] )
                        \\;=\;
                        \\big( d[\Gamma_1]  \big) \wedge [\Gamma_2]
                        +
                        (-1)^{deg(\Gamma_1)} [\Gamma_1] \wedge \big( d [\Gamma_2]\big)
                        \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Lemmas 6.11 - 6.14
            )
          %p
            %br/
          %h5#TheGraphComplex The graph complex
          #VanishingGraphs.num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              %strong (vanishing graphs)
            %p
              We say that a graph
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Graphs"}
              %em vanishing graph
              if it is one or more of the following:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole-diagram"} tadpole-diagram
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                  contains an edge
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(e) = t(e)
                  (Example
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GraphsWithDirectLoopsVanish"}
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+diagram"} vacuum diagram
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                  contains an internal vertex which is not connected, via some path of edges, to an external vertex;
              %li
                %p
                  it has
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+edges"} parallel edges
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                  contains a pair
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
                  of vertices, with more than one edge between them, i.e. if the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t)^{-1}\big\{(a,b)\big\}
                  contains more than one element.
              %li
                %p
                  it is less than trivalent:
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                  contains an internal vertex
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Verts
                          %mi int
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in Verts_{int}
                  that is less than trivalent, hence an internal vertex with less than 3 edges attached to it;
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                      %mi nil
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Graphs
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\widehat Graphs}^{nil}_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
                    \\;\subset\;
                    \\widehat Graphs_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3 \big)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              spanned by vanishing graphs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma]
              inside the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VectorSpaceOfGraphsWithSignRulesImposed"} (9)
              of all graphs.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Def. 6.16
            )
          #VanishingGraphsAreDifferentialIdeal.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_3 Lemma
            %p
              %strong (vanishing graphs form a differential ideal)
            %p
              The subspace of vanishing graphs (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanishingGraphs"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+ideal"} differential ideal
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebra"} differential graded-commutative algebra
              of all graphs (Lemma
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialProperties"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Lemma 6.17
            )
          %p This implises that the quotient of all graphs by the vanishing graphs is still a differential graded-commutative algebra:
          #GraphComplexDgcAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_11 Definition
            %p
              %strong (graph complex)
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %em graph complex
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              external vertices is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebra"} differential graded-commutative algebra
            #eq:TheGraphComplexAsQuotientByVanishingGraphs.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (12)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Graphs
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi Graphs
                            %mo ^
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mover
                            %mi Graphs
                            %mo ^
                          %mi n
                          %mi nil
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Graphs_n
                    \\big(
                    \\mathbb{R}^3
                    \\big)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\frac{
                    {\widehat Graphs}_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3\big)
                    }
                    {
                    {\widehat Graphs}^{nil}_n\big( \mathbb{R}^3\big)
                    }
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebra"} differential graded-commutative algebra
              of all graphs (Lemma
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialProperties"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+ideal"} differential ideal
              (Lemma
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanishingGraphsAreDifferentialIdeal"}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanishingGraphs"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"}> Lambrechts-Volić 14, Def. 6.19
            )
          #A9CocycleInGraphs3.num_example
            %h6#example_8 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (A 9-cocycle in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Graphs
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_3(\mathbb{R}^3)
            %p
              The trivalent graph of degree 9 from Example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivalenGraphs"}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Graphs
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_3(\mathbb{R}^3)
              (Def.
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GraphComplexDgcAlgebra"}
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/A9CocycleInGraphs3.jpg", :width => "610"}/
            %p
              The computation of the differential is just as for the 3-term relation in Example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ThreeTermRelation"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+edges"} parallel edges
              and hence are vanishing graphs (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanishingGraphs"}
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheGraphComplexAsQuotientByVanishingGraphs"} (12)
              defining the graph complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Graphs
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_3\big( \mathbb{R}^3 \big)
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GraphComplexDgcAlgebra"}
            %blockquote
              %p
                This trivalent diagram must be exact, as there is not supposed to be any cohomology in degree 9 (by Prop.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealCohomologyOfConfigurationSpaceOfOrderedPointsInEuclideanSpace"}
          #GraphsAreInNonNegativeDegree.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_4 Lemma
            %p
              %strong (graphs are in non-negative degree)
            %p
              For all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegreeOfAGraph"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma]
              in the graph complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Graphs
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GraphComplexDgcAlgebra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≥
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Graphs
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    deg\big( [\Gamma] \big)
                    \\;\geq\;
                    0
                    \\;\;
                    \\in
                    \\;\;
                    Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
                    \\,.
            %p Moreover, the only graphs of degree 0 are those containg the external vertices and nothing else:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext or
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Graphs
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    deg\big( [\Gamma]\big)
                    \=
                    0
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\Leftrightarrow\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    [\Gamma] = 0
                    \\;\;\;\text{or}\;\;\;
                    [\Gamma] = \big[ {}_1 \;\; {}_2 \;\; \cdots \;\; {}_n  \big]
                    \\;\;\;\;\in\;\;
                    Graphs_n(\mathbb{R}^3)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole"} tadpole
              graphs are vanishing graphs by Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanishingGraphs"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              has two distint vertices it ends on, for otherwise we have the zero element in the graph complex.
            %p
              Now, since each edge has degree 2 (according to Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegreeOfAGraph"}
            %p Since external vertices have degree 0, together with the half-edges that end on them they contribute a non-negative number to the total degree.
            %p
              While internal vertices have degree -3 (according to Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegreeOfAGraph"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanishingGraphs"}
            %p This proves the first claim.
            %p
              For the second claim, recall from Example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivalenGraphs"}
              that a graph has degree 0 precisely if it is a disjoint union of a) isolated external vertices and b) trivalent graphs all whose vertices are internal.
            %p
              But if there is any disjoint non-empty sub-graph with only internal vertices, the total graph is again a vanishing graph by Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanishingGraphs"}
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/VacuumDiagramVanishesInGraphComplex.jpg", :width => "610"}/
            %p Hence the only non-vanishing graphs of degree 0 are those which have some isolated external vertices and nothing else.
            %center
